@startuml
title Sales Forecasting — historical sales and EWMA forecast
autonumber

actor Owner
boundary "Forecasting View" as View
control "Store Context" as Store
control "Forecast Calculator" as Calculator
participant "Sales Orders" as Orders
participant "Inflow Transactions" as Transactions
participant "Product Catalog" as Products

== Obtain current data ==
activate Store
Store --> View: Live orders, transactions,\ncategories and products
deactivate Store
Owner -> View: Open forecasting or change period,\nhorizon or category
activate View
View -> Calculator: Recalculate selected forecast
activate Calculator
Calculator -> Orders: Read non-cancelled orders\nfor historical intervals
activate Orders
Orders --> Calculator: Order dates, totals and items
deactivate Orders
Calculator -> Products: Resolve product categories\nfor category-specific sales
activate Products
Products --> Calculator: Product category data
deactivate Products
opt No order sales for an interval and all categories selected
  Calculator -> Transactions: Read inflow transactions\nfor that interval
  activate Transactions
  Transactions --> Calculator: Transaction inflows
  deactivate Transactions
end
Calculator -> Calculator: Aggregate daily, weekly or monthly history
Calculator -> Calculator: Smooth history using EWMA (alpha = 0.3)
Calculator -> Calculator: Project smoothed value across horizon
Calculator --> View: Historical and forecast points
deactivate Calculator
View --> Owner: Render sales forecast chart
deactivate View

opt New order or transaction arrives
  Store --> View: Updated live sales data
  activate View
  View -> Calculator: Recalculate forecast
  activate Calculator
  Calculator --> View: Updated history and forecast
  deactivate Calculator
  View --> Owner: Refresh chart
  deactivate View
end
@enduml
